+# 百度网盘 Go — Android
+
+The Android client of **BaiduNetGo**, the Baidu Netdisk app whose desktop half is the
+Go/MyGo app at the repository root. It is a separate Gradle project: it does not
+build with `go build`, does not load the Go code, and can be built and released on its
+own. The user-facing design is Material 3 (Compose), with dynamic color, light/dark
+themes and a Chinese interface.
+
+## What it does
+
+- **扫码登录** — Baidu's QR sign-in (the code is shown as an image, the phone confirms it).
+- **备份（文件夹自动备份）** — pick local folders with the system picker (SAF), mirror
+  them into a netdisk folder (default `/备份`), incrementally, on a schedule
+  (仅手动 / 15 分钟 / 1 小时 / 6 小时 / 24 小时), in the background with WorkManager,
+  or immediately with live progress in a foreground service.
+- **相册备份** — pick which albums (MediaStore buckets, photos and videos) to back up,
+  with per-album counts, sizes and last-sync status; `/备份/相册/<album>/<file>`.
+- **加密备份** — OpenPGP symmetric encryption (passphrase) shared by both kinds of
+  backup: each uploaded file becomes `<name>.gpg`, decryptable with `gpg -d` on any
+  computer. The same format as the desktop app's backup (see `docs/BACKUP.md`), so
+  files from both devices restore with the same command.
+- **传输** — live uploads with progress, speed and cancel; recent runs with results.
+- **设置** — account and quota, upload concurrency, Wi-Fi-only, theme, passphrase,
+  about (version and the patched-build declaration crediting DeepSeek and GLM).
+
+## Modules
+
+| Module  | Type                         | Package                       | Purpose |
+|---------|------------------------------|-------------------------------|---------|
+| `:core` | Kotlin JVM (`kotlin("jvm")`) | `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core` | netdisk client (`net/`), OpenPGP (`crypto/`), backup engine (`backup/`) — no Android framework, unit-tested on the JVM |
+| `:app`  | `com.android.application`    | `com.pengstem.baidunetgo`      | Compose Material 3 UI, MediaStore albums, SAF folders, WorkManager, foreground service, Keystore storage |
+
+`:app` depends on `:core`. Business logic belongs in `:core` so it stays testable
+without a device. The API contract between the halves is `docs/CORE-API.md`.
+
+## Build
+
+Requirements: **JDK 21**, an Android SDK with **platform 37** and build-tools 36+,
+and a writable Gradle home. `compileSdk = 37`, `minSdk = 26`, `targetSdk = 37`,
+Java/Kotlin bytecode target 17.
+
+```bash
+export ANDROID_HOME=/path/to/android-sdk      # required (or sdk.dir in local.properties)
+export ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=$ANDROID_HOME         # some tools still read this
+export JAVA_HOME=/path/to/jdk-21              # required: JDK 21
+# optional: keep Gradle caches out of $HOME
+export GRADLE_USER_HOME=/path/to/gradle-home
+```
+
+Commands (run from this `android/` directory):
+
+```bash
+./gradlew :app:assembleDebug --console=plain    # build the debug APK
+./gradlew :core:test --console=plain            # JVM unit tests (netdisk, OpenPGP, backup)
+./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --console=plain # storage codec / path-rule tests
+./gradlew :app:lint --console=plain             # Android lint (HTML report below)
+```
+
+The APK lands at `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`; install it with
+
+```bash
+adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
+```
+
+Lint report: `app/build/reports/lint-results-debug.html`.
+
+### Offline / cached builds
+
+The wrapper uses `gradle-9.8.1-bin.zip` (unpacked under `$GRADLE_USER_HOME/wrapper/dists`).
+Dependencies come from `google()` and `mavenCentral()`; once the cache is warm,
+`--offline` works:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew --offline :app:assembleDebug
+```
+
+The shared toolchain Gradle home on this machine ships an init script that forces
+`--offline` globally (it was added for another project). `settings.gradle.kts` sets
+`gradle.startParameter.isOffline = false` so this project can resolve what is missing
+from the cache; remove that line on a machine that does not force offline mode.
+
+`gradle.properties` sets `kotlin.compiler.execution.strategy=in-process` because the
+sandbox `$HOME` is read-only and the Kotlin daemon cannot create its marker files under
+`~/.local/share/kotlin/daemon`. On a normal developer machine you may delete that line
+for faster incremental Kotlin compilation.
+
+## Tests
+
+- `:core:test` — 33 JVM tests: the netdisk client against **`cmd/fakepand`** (the Go fake
+  netdisk the desktop tests use; it is built on the fly and its `url=…` line read from
+  stdout, or `FAKEPAN_URL` points at an already-running one), OpenPGP against the real
+  `gpg` in both directions (`gpg --list-packets` checks the packet parameters), and the
+  backup engine against a fake `Netdisk`.
+- `:app:testDebugUnitTest` — encrypted-store codec and netdisk path rules.
+- There is **no emulator** on the machine this was developed on (no `/dev/kvm`), so
+  device tests are not part of the suite; `android/screenshots/` holds headless
+  Robolectric renders of the main screens when they could be produced.
+
+## Netdisk protocol
+
+`:core`'s client mirrors the desktop Go client (`internal/baidu`, `internal/pcsport`)
+exactly: the same pan.baidu.com web endpoints for listing, file-manager operations,
+quota and QR sign-in, and the same chunked upload (`/api/precreate` → `pcs/superfile2`
+parts → `/api/create`, 4 MiB parts with per-part MD5) — see `docs/CORE-API.md`. Keeping
+both halves on one protocol is why the same fake netdisk can test them.
+
+## Signing (development only)
+
+Debug builds are signed with **`keystore/dev.jks`**, committed on purpose so anyone can
+build: alias `baidunetgo`, store/key password `baidunetgo-dev`, validity 10000 days,
+`CN=BaiduNetGo Dev`.
+
+**Warning:** this is a *development* keystore with a public password. Never ship a
+release build with it and never reuse it for a published app; add a proper release
+signing configuration (environment variables / CI secrets) before distribution. It
+exists so builds never write to `~/.android`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+Versions are pinned in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`: AGP 9.4.1 (with its built-in
+Kotlin — do **not** apply `org.jetbrains.kotlin.android`), Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose BOM
+2026.09.00 (Material 3 1.4.0), activity-compose, lifecycle, WorkManager, DataStore,
+documentfile (SAF), Coil 3 (album covers), OkHttp 5, BouncyCastle bcpg (OpenPGP),
+kotlinx.serialization/coroutines, JUnit 4.
+
+To add a dependency, add a `[versions]` entry and a `[libraries]` alias to
+`gradle/libs.versions.toml`, then use it as `implementation(libs.foo)`; Compose
+versions come from the BOM.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+android/
+├── settings.gradle.kts, build.gradle.kts, gradle.properties
+├── gradle/libs.versions.toml, gradle/wrapper/
+├── gradlew, gradlew.bat, local.properties (git-ignored)
+├── keystore/dev.jks                  # dev-only signing key
+├── docs/CORE-API.md                  # :core ↔ :app contract
+├── screenshots/                      # headless renders (when produced)
+├── core/src/{main,test}/kotlin/com/pengstem/baidunetgo/core/
+│   ├── net/                          # BaiduApi, QrLogin, HTTP/JSON, models
+│   ├── crypto/                       # Pgp (BouncyCastle, gpg-compatible)
+│   └── backup/                       # incremental engine, sources, state store
+└── app/src/main/
+    ├── AndroidManifest.xml
+    ├── java/com/pengstem/baidunetgo/
+    │   ├── BaiduNetGoApplication.kt, MainActivity.kt
+    │   ├── data/                     # container, Keystore stores, settings,
+    │   │                             # MediaStore albums, SAF documents, runner,
+    │   │                             # scheduler, transfer history
+    │   ├── service/                  # foreground backup service, worker, notifications
+    │   └── ui/                       # theme, shell, view model, screens, components
+    └── res/                          # Chinese strings, icons, themes
+```
+
+All user-facing strings are Chinese and live in `res/values/strings.xml`; code
+comments are English.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- v1 is a backup client: it does not browse, download or preview the netdisk, and it
+  cannot restore a backup back to the phone (use `gpg -d` on a computer).
+- Changing the passphrase does not re-encrypt files already uploaded; the dialog warns.
+- Release builds are unsigned (only the dev debug keystore is configured).
