+# Android app — shared contract (core ↔ UI)
+
+This file is the contract between the two halves of the Android app. Both agents code
+against it; change it only if you must, and say so in your report.
+
+- `:core` (`android/core`) — pure-JVM Kotlin: Baidu netdisk client, OpenPGP, backup engine,
+  album planning models. **No Android framework imports** (`android.*`, `androidx.*`), so it
+  is unit-testable on the JVM. Package `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core`.
+- `:app` (`android/app`) — Android / Compose Material 3 UI, MediaStore, WorkManager,
+  notification, SAF pickers. Package `com.pengstem.baidunetgo`.
+
+Toolchain: AGP 9.4.1 (its built-in Kotlin; do **not** apply `org.jetbrains.kotlin.android`),
+Kotlin 2.4.20, Compose BOM 2026.09.00, compileSdk/targetSdk 37, minSdk 26, JDK 17 targets.
+Dependencies are already declared in `android/gradle/libs.versions.toml` (okhttp 5.5.1,
+bcpg 1.87, kotlinx-serialization-json 1.11.0, coroutines 1.11.0, work-runtime-ktx 2.11.2,
+lifecycle 2.11.0, datastore-preferences 1.2.1, coil-compose 3.6.3, icons-extended). Use
+those aliases; add new ones to the catalog only when truly needed.
+
+## 1. Netdisk client (`:core`)
+
+Mirror the desktop Go client in `internal/baidu` (read it: `list.go`, `ops.go`,
+`upload.go`, `qrlogin.go`, `user.go`) — same endpoints, same parameters, same
+cookie/bdstoken handling. The Kotlin code sends the same browser UA and
+`Referer: https://pan.baidu.com/`. Package: `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core.net`.
+
+These are the exact shipped signatures; `:app` codes against them.
+
+```kotlin
+data class Credentials(
+    val cookies: String,           // "BDUSS=…; STOKEN=…; …" as stored by the desktop app
+    val bduss: String,
+    val stoken: String,
+    val uid: Long? = null,
+    val name: String? = null,      // 百度昵称 when known
+)
+
+data class LoginStatus(val loggedIn: Boolean, val bdstoken: String, val vipType: Int)
+
+data class RemoteFile(
+    val name: String, val isDir: Boolean, val size: Long, val fsId: Long,
+    val md5: String,               // unscrambled, "" when the API gave none
+    val modified: Long,            // seconds
+)
+
+data class UserInfo(val name: String = "", val vipType: Int = 0, val used: Long = 0, val total: Long = 0)
+data class Quota(val used: Long = 0, val total: Long = 0)
+
+open class BaiduException(message: String, val errno: Int = 0) : IOException(message)
+class NotLoggedInException(
+    message: String = "登录已失效，请重新登录", errno: Int = -6,
+) : BaiduException(message, errno)
+
+// What the backup engine needs of a netdisk (tests stand in for it; BaiduApi implements it).
+interface Netdisk {
+    suspend fun list(dir: String, page: Int = 1, pageSize: Int = 1000): List<RemoteFile>
+    suspend fun mkdir(dir: String)
+    suspend fun upload(local: File, remote: String, connections: Int = 2,
+                       onProgress: (done: Long, total: Long) -> Unit = { _, _ -> })
+    // Stream upload: `open` hands out a fresh stream per call. BaiduApi overrides
+    // this to send parts straight from the streams (SAF documents have no File);
+    // the default implementation spools to a temp file and calls the File overload.
+    suspend fun upload(open: () -> InputStream, size: Long, remote: String, connections: Int = 2,
+                       onProgress: (done: Long, total: Long) -> Unit = { _, _ -> })
+}
+
+open class BaiduApi(
+    base: String = "https://pan.baidu.com",   // tests point it at fakepand
+    http: OkHttpClient = OkHttpClient(),
+) : Netdisk {
+    var credentials: Credentials?             // assigning it seeds the client's cookie jar
+    suspend fun loginStatus(): LoginStatus
+    suspend fun userInfo(): UserInfo          // name, vip level, quota used/total
+    suspend fun list(dir: String, page: Int = 1, pageSize: Int = 1000): List<RemoteFile>
+    suspend fun mkdir(dir: String)            // creates one folder; -8 "exists" counts as success
+    suspend fun delete(paths: List<String>)   // recycle bin; errno 0 is acceptance (async)
+    suspend fun quota(): Quota
+    suspend fun upload(local: File, remote: String, connections: Int = 2,
+                       onProgress: (done: Long, total: Long) -> Unit = { _, _ -> })
+    suspend fun upload(open: () -> InputStream, size: Long, remote: String, connections: Int = 2,
+                       onProgress: (done: Long, total: Long) -> Unit = { _, _ -> })
+    fun cookiesHeader(): String               // "BDUSS=…; STOKEN=…; …", what :app stores
+    fun snapshotCredentials(): Credentials?   // credentials + cookies the netdisk rotated in
+}
+```
+
+Cookie/bdstoken handling: one `CookieJar` per client. Everything in
+`Credentials.cookies` (and `bduss`/`stoken` on their own) is loaded into it when
+`credentials` is assigned, so a QR or cookie sign-in works with the very next
+call, and `cookiesHeader()` returns what should be persisted. `loginStatus()`
+fetches the `bdstoken` every write needs and records `uid`/name on `credentials`.
+If a write answers `errno` -6, -4 or 111 the cached token is dropped and
+`NotLoggedInException` (message 登录已失效，请重新登录) is thrown, so the next
+write fetches a fresh token.
+
+Upload protocol (must match `internal/pcsport/upload.go` and the fake in `cmd/fakepand`):
+`POST /api/precreate` (form `path`, `size`, `isdir`, `autoinit=1`, `rtype=3`,
+`block_list` JSON array of per-part MD5 hex) → `uploadid` + `block_list` of parts
+already present; for each missing part
+`POST {pcsHost}/rest/2.0/pcs/superfile2?method=upload&type=tmpfile&path=…&partseq=i&uploadid=…&vip=1`
+multipart field `file` (pcs host from `GET /rest/2.0/pcs/file?method=locateupload`);
+then `POST /api/create` with `path`, `size`, `isdir=0`, `rtype`, `uploadid`,
+`block_list` = the MD5 of every part in partseq order. Part size 4 MiB
+(`baidupcs.MinUploadBlockSize`); MD5 is computed in a streaming pass over the
+source (a 256 KiB buffer, never the whole file) and then each part is streamed
+from a fresh source stream straight into the request body. Parts the answer lists
+as present are skipped; the rest go over `connections` parallel requests; a failed
+part is retried twice (250 ms, 500 ms) and a part the netdisk refuses outright, a
+short read or a returned MD5 that does not match fails the upload with a clear
+Chinese message. Progress callbacks are throttled to at most four a second, plus a
+final 100 %. `return_type == 2` means the netdisk already had the content.
+
+QR sign-in (`mirror internal/baidu/qrlogin.go`, JSONP bodies must be unwrapped):
+`GET https://passport.baidu.com/v2/api/getqrcode?lp=pc&qrloginfrom=pc&gid=<guid>&apiver=v3&tt=<ms>&tpl=netdisk&_=<ms>`
+→ `{imgurl, sign}` (the image is already a QR PNG; download it); poll
+`GET /channel/unicast?channel_id=<sign>&gid=<guid>&tpl=netdisk&apiver=v3&callback=&tt=&_=`
+→ `channel_v` JSON `{status,v}` (0 confirmed, 1 scanned, 2 cancelled); then
+`GET /v3/login/main/qrbdusslogin?v=<ms>&bduss=<v>&u=https://pan.baidu.com/disk/home&loginVersion=v4&qrcode=1&tpl=netdisk&apiver=v3&tt=&traceid=&callback=`
+and `GET /v3/login/api/auth/?return_type=5&tpl=netdisk&u=<home>` to obtain
+`BDUSS`/`STOKEN` from the cookie jar. Expose:
+
+```kotlin
+class QrLogin(
+    http: OkHttpClient = OkHttpClient(),
+    passportBase: String = "https://passport.baidu.com",   // tests only
+) {
+    suspend fun start(): ByteArray                 // QR PNG bytes (already encoded)
+    suspend fun poll(): QrState                    // one poll; call again about a second later
+    suspend fun finish(): Credentials              // throws BaiduException when STOKEN is missing
+}
+enum class QrState { Waiting, Scanned, Confirmed, Expired }
+```
+
+A poll that hits a network hiccup reads as `Waiting`; a code older than three
+minutes or cancelled on the phone reads as `Expired` (call `start()` again). When
+the sign-in only yields `BDUSS` (no `STOKEN`), `finish()` throws a clear error
+telling the user to sign in with cookies instead.
+
+## 2. OpenPGP (`:core`)
+
+Package `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core.crypto`, BouncyCastle `bcpg` only (no JCE
+provider to install). Exact shipped API:
+
+```kotlin
+class PgpException(message: String, cause: Throwable? = null) : Exception(message, cause)
+
+object Pgp {
+    const val Suffix = ".gpg"
+    fun encrypt(dst: OutputStream, src: InputStream, passphrase: CharArray)
+    fun decrypt(dst: OutputStream, src: InputStream, passphrase: CharArray)
+    fun encryptFile(dst: File, src: File, passphrase: CharArray): Long   // bytes written
+    fun decryptFile(dst: File, src: File, passphrase: CharArray): Long   // bytes written
+}
+```
+
+Format: decryptable by the desktop app's Go `internal/pgp` **and** by real gpg 2.4
+— binary OpenPGP, symmetric (passphrase only), AES-256 (`cipher 9`), iterated+salted
+S2K with SHA-256 (`s2k 3, hash 8`), count 4194304 (encoded byte `0xC0`, exactly what
+`gpg --s2k-count 4194304` emits), **no compression**, integrity-protected SEIPD v1
+(`mdc_method: 2`), binary literal data with an empty file-name hint. The v4 SKESK
+carries no encrypted session key (the S2K-derived key is the session key), which is
+also the form gpg itself writes.
+
+Streaming both ways through one 256 KiB buffer; no temp files. `decrypt` is a single
+streaming pass, so on a wrong passphrase bytes may already have reached `dst` before
+the MDC check fails (it still throws `PgpException`). `decryptFile` is what callers
+that must never see partial plaintext use: it first verifies passphrase + MDC with
+the output discarded, then writes the real file, and removes it on failure. The file
+variants flush/close their own handles, leave no partial file behind, and return the
+number of bytes written.
+
+## 3. Backup engine (`:core`)
+
+Two sources, one engine. A "backup set" mirrors local files into a netdisk folder,
+incrementally, optionally encrypted. Package `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core.backup`.
+
+```kotlin
+open class BackupException(message: String, cause: Throwable? = null) : IOException(message, cause)
+
+val defaultExcludes: Set<String>       // .git, node_modules, .cache, .Trash, .DS_Store,
+                                       // Thumbs.db, and the "~$" marker (prefix match)
+
+data class SourceFile(
+    val relativePath: String,        // "2024/a.jpg" — no leading slash, '/' separated
+    val size: Long,
+    val lastModified: Long,          // millis
+    val open: () -> InputStream,     // fresh stream per call; caller closes
+)
+interface BackupSource { val label: String; fun files(): List<SourceFile> }
+
+class FolderSource(
+    val root: File,
+    val exclude: Set<String> = defaultExcludes,
+    override val label: String = root.name,
+) : BackupSource
+// JVM/Android app-private folders; SAF trees are implemented in :app as a BackupSource.
+
+data class BackupConfig(
+    val dest: String,                // netdisk folder, e.g. "/备份"
+    val encrypt: Boolean = false,
+    val parallel: Int = 2,           // uploads at once, clamped 1..4
+    val remoteName: String,          // folder under dest; e.g. "相册/相机" (slashes optional)
+)
+
+data class BackupProgress(
+    val label: String, val file: String, val remote: String,
+    val done: Long, val total: Long,
+    val uploaded: Int, val skipped: Int, val failed: Int,
+)
+data class BackupResult(val uploaded: Int, val skipped: Int, val failed: Int, val bytes: Long,
+                        val errors: List<String>)
+
+data class StateEntry(val size: Long, val lastModified: Long, val remote: String = "")
+data class BackupState(val version: Int = 1, val entries: Map<String, StateEntry> = emptyMap())
+class BackupStateStore(val path: String) {           // atomic 0600 JSON, tolerant of garbage
+    fun load(): BackupState                          // missing/corrupt file ⇒ empty state
+    fun save(state: BackupState)                     // temp file + rename, 0600 on POSIX
+}
+object Backup {
+    suspend fun run(
+        api: Netdisk,                // pass the real BaiduApi; tests pass a fake
+        source: BackupSource, config: BackupConfig,
+        state: BackupStateStore, passphrase: CharArray?,
+        onProgress: (BackupProgress) -> Unit = {},
+    ): BackupResult
+}
+```
+
+Rules: skip a file whose `"<label>|<relativePath>"` is in the state with the same
+size and lastModified; never delete anything on either side; create the remote
+folders as needed (only after a listing shows they are missing, remembering what was
+created in this run); retries are left to the next run; failures are collected, not
+fatal; cancellation is `CancellationException` and still saves the state for
+finished files. `dest`/`remoteName` may carry leading or trailing slashes — remote
+paths are normalised. Encrypted uploads use a unique temp file under
+`java.io.tmpdir`, uploaded as `<remote>.gpg`, removed in a `finally`; at most
+`parallel` exist. An empty passphrase with `encrypt = true` throws
+`BackupException` (加密备份口令不能为空). Progress is throttled to ≤ 4/s per file and
+carries cumulative counters.
+
+Album backup uses the same engine with `BackupSource` = the photos of one album and
+`remoteName = "相册/<album name>"`; the album scanner itself lives in `:app` (MediaStore).
+
+## 4. `:app` structure
+
+`MainActivity` → `BaiduNetGoApp` (already scaffolded) with a `NavigationBar` of four tabs
+(备份 / 相册备份 / 传输 / 设置) and a sign-in screen shown while there is no session.
+State: one `AppViewModel` (manual DI, `AndroidViewModel`, `StateFlow<UiState>`), all IO on
+`Dispatchers.IO`, no blocking on the main thread, `collectAsStateWithLifecycle` in Compose.
+
+- **登录** — QR image, 状态文字 (等待扫码 / 已扫描，请在手机上确认 / 已取消 / 已过期, 刷新), then the
+  four tabs. Credentials and the backup passphrase are stored via Android Keystore
+  (AES-GCM) + DataStore/JSON in `filesDir`, never in plain prefs.
+- **备份** — auto folder backup: 自动备份 switch, 备份到 (netdisk path, default `/备份`),
+  添加文件夹 (SAF `ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT_TREE`, persisted URI permission, shows the chosen tree
+  name), list of chosen folders with per-folder status (上次备份 / 文件数 / 错误), 移除,
+  间隔 (仅手动 / 15 分钟 / 1 小时 / 6 小时 / 24 小时), 加密备份 switch + 密码 (set/change dialog,
+  ≥ 8 chars), 立即备份 / 取消 with live progress (file + percent + counts), 上次结果 and error
+  details.
+- **相册备份** — album list from MediaStore (`Images` **and** `Videos`, bucket = album) with
+  cover thumbnail (Coil), name, count and total size; a checkbox per album (default: all
+  selected), 全选/全不选, 仅 WiFi switch, 自动备份相册 switch, 立即备份/取消 with progress,
+  加密相册 switch sharing the same passphrase, and per-album last-synced status. Uploads go
+  to `/备份/相册/<album>`; encrypted files keep the `.gpg` suffix (e.g. `IMG_0001.jpg.gpg`).
+- **传输** — running and recent uploads: name, source (文件夹/相册), progress bar, speed,
+  cancel button; finished items with ✓/error.
+- **设置** — account (昵称/会员/容量, 退出登录), 加密口令 set/change, 上传并发 (1–4), 仅 WiFi,
+  dark-mode (system/light/dark), 关于 (version, 修复版声明 credited to DeepSeek and GLM, build
+  info), and a short note that the desktop app writes the same `.gpg` files.
+
+Scheduling: `WorkManager` periodic workers (folder backup and album backup, minimum 15 min,
+configurable interval, `NetworkType.UNMETERED` when 仅 WiFi is on, exponential backoff), plus
+a foreground `Service` (with progress notification) for user-initiated runs so long backups
+survive; cancel must stop the work promptly.
+
+Permissions: `INTERNET`, `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE`, `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` (33+, ask at first run),
+`READ_MEDIA_IMAGES`/`READ_MEDIA_VIDEO` (33+) or `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` (≤ 32), `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC`.
+"相册备份" asks for media permission lazily and explains why.
+
+## 5. Tests
+
+`:core` unit tests (JVM, run by `./gradlew :core:test`):
+- netdisk client against the real Go fake netdisk: start `cmd/fakepand` (built once with `go build
+  -o <tmp>/fakepand ./cmd/fakepand` from the repository root, `GOPATH`/`GOMODCACHE`/`GOCACHE`/
+  `GOFLAGS` exported) or use an already-running one from `FAKEPAN_URL`; read `url=…` from its
+  stdout; then exercise loginStatus/list/mkdir/upload (multi-part)/delete and assert with the
+  fake's `/api/list`, `/file` (bounded `Range` only) and `/api/recycle/list` endpoints.
+  `BaiduApi(base = "http://127.0.0.1:<port>")` points at it; any credentials are accepted.
+  The helper (test sources, `FakePand.kt`) keeps the fake's stderr request log, so a test can
+  count `/rest/2.0/pcs/superfile2` requests (a 9 MiB upload must be three parts). Skip the test
+  cleanly when neither the env var nor `go` is available.
+- PGP: Kotlin encrypt → `gpg --batch --pinentry-mode loopback --passphrase … -d` decrypts to the
+  same bytes; `gpg --symmetric --cipher-algo AES256 --s2k-digest-algo SHA256 --s2k-count 4194304`
+  output → `Pgp.decryptFile` matches; `gpg --list-packets` confirms cipher 9, `s2k 3, hash 8`,
+  count 4194304, `mdc_method: 2`, a literal packet and no compression (skip when gpg is absent,
+  always use a throw-away `GNUPGHOME`).
+- backup engine: fake `Netdisk` + temp dir sources covering first run, skip-unchanged, changed
+  file, nested folders, exclusions, encryption (`.gpg` name + temp file gone), failure keeps
+  going, cancellation, state round-trip.
+
+`:app`: `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` must build, `:app:lint` must not fail the build.
+Screenshots without an emulator are a stretch goal (Robolectric + Compose UI test, write PNGs
+to `android/screenshots/`); skip rather than fight it if it costs too much time.
+
+## 6. Performance requirements (both halves)
+
+- Never buffer a file: stream uploads from the source `InputStream` to the network in 4 MiB
+  parts, computing MD5 on the fly; encryption also streams.
+- IO on `Dispatchers.IO`, CPU work on `Dispatchers.Default`, bounded parallelism
+  (`Semaphore`), progress callbacks throttled to ≤ 4/s.
+- Compose: stable keys in `LazyColumn`/`LazyVerticalGrid`, `remember`/`derivedStateOf` instead
+  of recomputing lists per frame, no work in composables that touches disk or network,
+  Coil with memory+disk cache for thumbnails.
+- The album list must be paged/aggregated in one MediaStore query per album kind, not per album.
